  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2004-p15.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let Jack be \\(10x + y\\) and Bill be \\(10y + x.\\) Then \\(10x + y + 5 = 2(10y + x + 5),\\) so \\(8x = 19y + 5.\\) Testing digits, only \\(y = 1, x = 3\\) works, so Jack is \\(31\\) and Bill is \\(13.\\) The difference is \\(31 - 13 = 18.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Let Jack be \\(10x + y\\) and Bill be \\(10y + x\\)",
        "\\(10x + y + 5 = 2(10y + x + 5)\\) simplifies to \\(8x = 19y + 5\\)"
      ],
